@startuml
' --- General Configuration ---
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing true

' --- Class Definitions ---

' [System Manager & Controller]
class SensorManagerNode {
    -initConverters()
    -timer_callback()
    -pointcloud_pubs_ : unordered_map
    -buffers_ : tSensorBuffer
    .. Responsibility ..
    Manages ROS 2 comms,
    sensor data buffering,
    and periodic conversion loop.
}

' [Object Creation Encapsulation]
class CloudConverterFactory {
    +static create(type, config) : CloudConverterPtr
}

' [Abstraction Interface - Base Class]
interface CloudConverterStrategy {
    #node_ptr_
    +convert(sensor_msg)
    +pc_convert_impl(sensor_msg)*
    .. Responsibility ..
    Abstracts conversion logic.
    Defines interface for sensor-specific
    implementation via pc_convert_impl.
}

class MonoTofCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}
class MultiTofCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}
class CameraCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}
class BottomIrCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}
class CollisionCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}
class EmptyCloudConverter {
    -pc_convert_impl()
}

' [Spatial Transformation Utility]
class FrameConverter {
    +tfSensor2RobotFrame()
    .. Responsibility ..
    Handles mathematical operations
    for Sensor -> Robot -> Global frame.
}

' [Message Builder & Serializer]
class PointCloudGenerator {
    +generatePointCloud2Message()
    +mergePointCloud2Vector()
    .. Responsibility ..
    Serializes calculated points into
    standard ROS 2 PointCloud2 format.
}

' --- Relationships & Notes ---

' [1] Dependency: Separation of creation responsibility
SensorManagerNode ..> CloudConverterFactory : uses
note bottom of CloudConverterFactory
  **Factory Pattern**
  Decouples Node from concrete types.
  Creates objects based on runtime config.
end note

' [2] Composition: Lifecycle management
SensorManagerNode "1" *-- "many" CloudConverterStrategy : owns
note on link
  **Composition**
  Node manages lifecycle of all converters.
  Converters are destroyed with the Node.
end note

' [3] Creation: Dynamic polymorphism
CloudConverterFactory ..> CloudConverterStrategy : instantiates
note right of CloudConverterFactory
  **Polymorphism**
  Returns concrete strategy objects
  as abstract interface types.
end note

' [4] Inheritance: Strategy Pattern implementation
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- MonoTofCloudConverter
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- MultiTofCloudConverter
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- CameraCloudConverter
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- BottomIrCloudConverter
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- CollisionCloudConverter
CloudConverterStrategy <|-- EmptyCloudConverter
note top of CloudConverterStrategy
  **Strategy Pattern**
  Decouples conversion behavior from
  specific sensor hardware algorithms.
end note

' [5] Association: Delegation of utility functions
CloudConverterStrategy --> FrameConverter : delegates TF
CloudConverterStrategy --> PointCloudGenerator : delegates PC2
note bottom of FrameConverter
  **Separation of Concerns**
  Isolates TF math and msg serialization
  to enhance reusability.
end note

' --- Summary of Pros & Cons (Technical Assessment) ---
legend right
  |= Pros |= Cons |
  | 1. Scalability: Minimal Node modification | 1. Slight overhead due to virtual calls |
  | 2. Flexibility: Runtime YAML configuration | 2. Increased architectural complexity |
  |<back:lightskyblue>**Performance Countermeasure**</back>| Modern compilers use Devirtualization. |
  | | Processing bottleneck is math, not calls. |
end legend

@endum